      "source_unit_id": "ibn_hajar_isabah_v1:arabic:v08:p0353:e6c1cc9510087de4",
      "arabic": "١١٨٨٢- وسناء بنت الصّلت السلمية\nذكر ابن ماكولا أن النّبي ﵌ تزوج بها فماتت قبل الدخول، كذا في «التّجريد»، وقد ذكرها ابن أبي خيثمة (وابن أبي عبدة) «١»، وسمّي جدّها الصّلت.\nوقال عبد القاهر بن السّريّ: اسمها سنا- يعني بغير واو. وقال قتادة: اسمها أسماء، وقد تقدم جميع ذلك.",
      "english": "11882—Wasna bint al-Salt al-Sulamiyya\n\nIbn Makula mentioned that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, married her, but she died before the marriage was consummated. Thus it appears in al-Tajrid. Ibn Abi Khaythama (and Ibn Abi Abda) [1] also mentioned her, and her grandfather is named al-Salt.\n\nAbd al-Qahir ibn al-Sari said: Her name was Sana—that is, without a waw. Qatada said: Her name was Asma. All of this has already been mentioned.",
      "arabic_sha256": "bad310364ef1f0c9127053521625152a0fd36464d56818dd890fbccfd95b19c7",
